From: Queqiongtao <467500670@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sun4i-codec: expose suniv headphone PA enable

The suniv F1C100s/F1C200s Class-D headphone output has an audible
hiss/squeak even when the DAC is fed digital silence.  Clearing HPPAEN
powers the output stage down and removes that noise.

Expose HPPAEN as a "Headphone PA Enable" control so userspace can power
the PA down across silent passages and bring it back when audio returns.

An earlier attempt to trigger the BIAS/DA16 calibration at 0x30 was
dropped: the trigger bit does not self-clear on this silicon, while the
boot ROM already programs the ADDA_TUNE/BIAS_CAL1 values.  The PA power
control is the reliable fix for the silent-scene noise.
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
@@ -1395,6 +1395,15 @@
 		   SUNIV_CODEC_OM_DACA_CTRL,
 		   SUNIV_CODEC_OM_DACA_CTRL_LHPPAMUTE,
 		   SUNIV_CODEC_OM_DACA_CTRL_RHPPAMUTE, 1, 0),
+	/*
+	 * Direct control of the headphone PA enable (HPPAEN).  DAPM also
+	 * drives this bit when the playback path is powered; exposing it
+	 * lets userspace power the PA down across silent passages, which
+	 * removes the suniv Class-D output-stage idle noise.
+	 */
+	SOC_SINGLE("Headphone PA Enable",
+		   SUNIV_CODEC_OM_DACA_CTRL,
+		   SUNIV_CODEC_OM_DACA_CTRL_HPPAEN, 1, 0),
 	SOC_SINGLE_TLV("Line In Playback Volume",
 		       SUNIV_CODEC_ADC_ACTL, SUNIV_CODEC_ADC_LINEINVOL,
 		       0x7, 0, suniv_codec_out_mixer_pregain_scale),
